1
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:26,000
Scooby-Doo! Shaggy's Showdown is a animation, family,
mystery film directed by Matt Peters.

2
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:46,000
When the Scooby gang visits a dude ranch, they discover that it and the nearby town have been
haunted by a ghostly cowboy, Dapper Jack, who fires real fire from his fire irons.

3
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:06,000
The mystery only deepens when it’s discovered that the ghost is
also the long lost relative of Shaggy Rogers!

4
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:26,000
Scooby-Doo / Fred (voice), played by Frank Welker.

5
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:46,000
Daphne (voice), played by Grey DeLisle.

6
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:06,000
Shaggy (voice), played by Matthew Lillard.

7
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:26,000
Velma (voice), played by Kate Micucci.

8
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:46,000
Larry (voice), played by Carlos Alazraqui.

9
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Buddy G. (voice), played by Max Charles.

10
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:26,000
Scooby-Doo!

11
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Shaggy's Showdown is a 2017 direct-to-DVD animated western comedy mystery film, and the
twenty-eighth entry in the direct-to-video series of Scooby-Doo films.

12
01:04:00,000 --> 01:04:06,000
It was released digitally on January 31, 2017, and on DVD on February 14, 2017.

13
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:26,000
The film explores themes of friendship, ranch, talking dog, cowboy, ghost.

14
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
The tone is lighthearted and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
